{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"length","index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"People run language models on their own computers because the cloud is not always the best fit. The most obvious reason is privacy: prompts can contain private notes, customer data, medical details, legal drafts, or unreleased ideas. Keeping the model local means that text does not have to leave the machine, which matters for individuals, small teams, and organizations with strict data rules.\n\nCost is another factor. Cloud APIs are convenient, but usage can grow quickly—especially for heavy experimentation, repeated testing, or high-volume workflows. A local model can turn a recurring per-token bill into a one-time hardware expense, though it also requires upfront investment and maintenance.\n\nLocal models also offer control. Users can choose the model, adjust settings, fine-tune it, inspect its behavior, and keep a record of what ran and when. That matters for developers, researchers, writers, and hobbyists who want to experiment without depending on a provider’s roadmap or pricing changes.\n\nLatency and reliability can also favor local execution. When a connection is slow, unreliable, or unavailable, an offline model still works. For some tasks, that independence is more valuable than the convenience of a hosted service.\n\nNone of this means local models are universally better. They usually require more technical skill, more hardware, and more care. But for many people, the appeal is simple: running a language model on their own computer gives them more control over their data, their costs, and their workflow. The cloud remains","reasoning_content":"The user asks for a short essay in English about why people run language models on their own computers instead of in the cloud. Need produce final essay. Need ensure accuracy: reasons include privacy/data control, cost for high usage, latency/offline, customization/fine-tuning, independence from providers, security/compliance, experimentation, reliability. Need be concise. No need for citations. Need maybe mention tradeoffs briefly. Need answer only essay. Ensure not overclaim: cloud has advantages; local has constraints. Short essay maybe 4-6 paragraphs or one cohesive ~300 words. Need final only.\n\nNeed consider if any safety? No.\n\nLet's craft polished short essay. Title optional. Mention not because cloud is bad but because local fits needs. Include privacy, cost, control, latency, offline, customization, trust. Mention hardware limits and maintenance. Keep concise."}}],"created":1795504514,"model":"/models/unsloth/Inkling-2-Mini-GGUF/Inkling-2-Mini-UD-IQ4_XS.gguf","system_fingerprint":"b12651-d426a3774","object":"chat.completion","usage":{"completion_tokens":512,"prompt_tokens":37,"total_tokens":549,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0}},"id":"chatcmpl-NspxcVtbxL3qm3xkyzU00Yrr45OEL6qa","timings":{"cache_n":0,"prompt_n":37,"prompt_ms":852.238,"prompt_per_token_ms":23.03345945945946,"prompt_per_second":43.41510235403725,"predicted_n":512,"predicted_ms":23308.041,"predicted_per_token_ms":45.612604696673195,"predicted_per_second":21.923764421042506}}
